    "answer": {
      "short": "$98\\pi\\text{ cm}^2$",
      "worked": "The square’s diagonal is the circle’s diameter, so halve it to find the radius.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}d^2 &= 14^2+14^2=392\\\\d &= \\sqrt{392}\\text{ cm}\\\\r &= \\frac{d}{2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{392}}{2}\\text{ cm}\\\\A &= \\pi\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{392}}{2}\\right)^2\\\\A &= \\pi\\left(\\frac{392}{4}\\right)\\\\A &= 98\\pi\\text{ cm}^2\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
